      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m using the term \"address space\" here in a bit abstract sense, i.e. the set of all unique addresses, independently of a particular representation of those addresses (normalized vs canonical). For example, \"we want to walk the entire address space in fix_hyp_mmu_page_refcnt()\" - that is our goal, regardless of which representation we choose.\n\n\u003e for ranges that span both the lower and the upper halves of the canonical address range\n\nSuch ranges don\u0027t exist? (Which is precisely the problem described here: canonical addressing doesn\u0027t allow address ranges spanning arbitrary continuous areas of the address space, while normalized addressing does allow that.)",
